    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Our Treatment Approach in Dublin CA"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "We start off by reviewing the results of your sleep study from your medical doctor. Then we customise treatment options with the goal of restorative sleep and better quality of life. Our dental team works with your sleep physician or respiratory medicine specialist if needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "One of the main tools is oral appliance therapy, an oral appliance that pulls your jaw slightly forward to open the airway, prevent snoring and let you breathe smoothly throughout the night. Some cases may still use continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) or be combined with weight loss to reduce risk factors."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Key features:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Diagnose and treat sleep disorders such as obstructive sleep apnea."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Use appliances instead of or alongside a CPAP machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Address common symptoms like interrupted sleep, loud snoring, daytime fatigue."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Monitor oxygen levels, jaw position, and airway space."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Collaborate with sleep medicine and sleep physician for whole-system care."
    },
    {
