      "type": "h2",
      "text": "How We Design the Right Sleep Apnea Treatment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Our team begins by reviewing your sleep study results or arranging one if you haven’t had it done. Once diagnosed, we suggest treatment approaches based on your pattern — whether it’s obstructive sleep apnea, central sleep apnea, or mixed types. A small change in jaw alignment can often make a big difference."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Most treating sleep apnea cases here rely on oral appliance therapy. It’s a custom device you wear while sleeping, a simple oral appliance that holds your jaw forward, keeping your airway open throughout the night."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The idea is to prevent your tongue and soft tissues from collapsing backward. Feels strange at first, but within a few nights, patients often say they slept peacefully for the first time in years. That’s how it should be."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start Your Sleep Apnea Treatment Today",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "tracy-ca-orthodontic-office-contact.php",
          "text": "Start Your Sleep Apnea Treatment Today"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Why Choose Us as Your Sleep Apnea Dentist in Dublin"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "We are a specialist practice that treats sleep apnea with the same precision we treat teeth and jaws. We know that the jaw, mouth and airway link strongly to breathing and nighttime comfort."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Our patients appreciate that we explain treatment in plain language, schedule efficiently, and adjust plans to how you respond physically. We don’t just hand over a device and send you home. We monitor and follow up to make sure you get better sleep and improved health."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "assets/img/dublin/img4.jpg",
      "alt": "Thumb",
      "title": null
    },
